Subject: harfbuzz: do not build the cairo integration

harfbuzz's cairo support is for its own utilities (hb-view and friends), which
this configuration does not build. The shaping API that consumers use does not
involve cairo, and WebKit depends on harfbuzz and cairo separately rather than
on the bridge between them.

Leaving it enabled makes meson search for cairo and, failing to find it, fall
through to a wrap-based subproject download that Buildroot disables:

  meson.build:194:16: ERROR: Automatic wrap-based subproject downloading is disabled

so a cairo that is built but not visible to pkg-config becomes a hard build
failure over a feature nothing uses.

WHY cairo was invisible to pkg-config has since been found, and it was not
harfbuzz's fault: the DDK's egl.pc declared Requires: x11 dri2proto glproto
xext xdamage xfixes xxf86vm, cairo-gl put "Requires: egl" into cairo.pc, and
pkg-config resolves Requires transitively and then fails -- so every
`pkg-config cairo` in the tree errored out naming X11. sgx545-um now strips
those lines at install time.

That makes this patch very likely redundant. It is kept for now because
removing it cannot be tested incrementally: harfbuzz is already built in the
output cache, so dropping the patch would change nothing until the next
from-scratch build. Drop it there and see whether harfbuzz finds cairo on its
own -- if it does, delete this file.

--- a/package/harfbuzz/harfbuzz.mk	2026-08-28 15:18:08
+++ b/package/harfbuzz/harfbuzz.mk	2026-08-28 15:18:08
@@ -44,12 +44,21 @@
 	-Dexperimental_api=false \
 	-Dfuzzer_ldflags=""
 
-ifeq ($(BR2_PACKAGE_CAIRO),y)
-HARFBUZZ_DEPENDENCIES += cairo
-HARFBUZZ_CONF_OPTS += -Dcairo=enabled
-else
+# harfbuzz's cairo integration exists for its own utilities (hb-view and
+# friends), which this configuration does not build. The library API that
+# consumers actually use -- shaping -- does not involve cairo at all, and
+# WebKit depends on harfbuzz and cairo separately rather than on the bridge
+# between them.
+#
+# Keeping it enabled means meson looks for cairo and, if it cannot see it,
+# falls through to a wrap-based subproject download, which Buildroot disables:
+#
+#   meson.build:194:16: ERROR: Automatic wrap-based subproject downloading
+#                              is disabled
+#
+# so a cairo that is present but not visible to pkg-config turns into a hard
+# failure over a feature nothing uses.
 HARFBUZZ_CONF_OPTS += -Dcairo=disabled
-endif
 
 ifeq ($(BR2_PACKAGE_FREETYPE),y)
 HARFBUZZ_DEPENDENCIES += freetype
